  "verdict": "GO -- the CONTENT words of the EMERGE-frame render are now PRODUCED ON SPIKES. The spiking-Broca producer's `spell` callback is the VALIDATED A->W read-out (`concept_speak_demo`): each CONTENT slot (subject/verb = the emergent concepts) is spelled by DRIVING the word's concept pool on a real SimulationBridge and DECODING the spoken word from `language_output` SPIKES. Content-slot spike-spell accuracy 1.000 over the EMERGE frames (>= 0.9); the A->W engine spells 16/16 content words correctly (raw A->W rate 1.000). GENUINELY SPIKING: the read-out reads cp_firing_states[language_output], and the LESION control (zeroing the pool->language_output pathway) COLLAPSES the decode to 0.097 (a host lookup would be unaffected -> the words are decoded FROM SPIKES). NO regression: the neural spell reproduces the token spell on the content slots (0 mismatches; the token-spell default path is byte-identical). The gate-first no-confab MOAT holds BY CONSTRUCTION: 0 spell calls + 0 producer invocations on abstains (the producer -- and hence the A->W read-out -- is NEVER invoked on an abstain). 6 seeds. ==> the EMERGE-frame render is now FULLY SPIKING for the CONTENT slots (the ORDER was already spiking via EMERGE-59/63; the WORDS are now spiking via A->W). HONEST SCOPE: the DET/FUNC (function-word) slots keep the token surface -- the named closed-class-A->W follow-on (their pools are the EMERGE-62 discovered closed class). The A->W engine is GPU-trained ONCE at the validated scale + cached (a scale/data lever, not a new mechanism); the producer content vocab is 16 words rebound onto the 16 validated pools (reuse-by-import; NO sim/ edit). Renders the BOUNDED EMERGE frame inventory, NOT open prose (R4).",
